    "status": "confirmed",
    "reasoning": "q-51072: Both one-sided limits at x=1 equal 3, whereas f(1)=0. Thus f is discontinuous and not differentiable at 1, so it is not differentiable throughout (-2,2). Statements I and II are false; III is true. This confirms the earlier answer.\nq-72733: Subtracting x-y=2 from 2x-y=1 gives x=-1, then y=-3. Option 3 uses the correct inverse matrix and evaluates to the column vector (-1,-3), agreeing with the captured solution and the earlier answer. The source uses x for the entire solution vector, although x also denotes its first scalar coordinate.",
